# =================================================================
# AutoTech AI Car Mechanic Chatbot — Frontend Environment Variables
# =================================================================

# 1. Local Development (Default)
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000/api
BACKEND_API_URL=http://localhost:8000/api

# 2. Production Deployment (e.g. Vercel connecting to AWS EC2 Backend)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://13.234.4.236/api
# BACKEND_API_URL=http://13.234.4.236/api
#
# NOTE ON PLAIN HTTP BACKEND & NEXT.JS PROXY ARCHITECTURE:
# When the Next.js frontend is served over HTTPS on Vercel, direct browser fetch
# calls to a plain HTTP backend (http://13.234.4.236/api) are blocked by modern
# browsers as 'Mixed Content'.
# To seamlessly resolve this without requiring a custom domain or SSL certificate on EC2,
# the frontend automatically detects HTTPS in src/services/api.ts and routes client calls
# to the same-origin proxy route (/api/backend/*).
# The Next.js server-side route handler then proxies requests securely to BACKEND_API_URL
# using server-to-server HTTP (which is not subject to browser Mixed Content blocking)
# while forwarding headers like X-Client-Token intact.
